ote about congenital sucrase-isomaltase deficiency in a pediatric gastroenterology journal.", "ROMAGNUOLE J:Romagnuole J is an author recognized for contributions to the field of gastroenterology, specifically focusing on the use of breath tests. They have participated in a study that examines the application of breath tests within gastroenterology practices and have also conducted a review of these tests, highlighting their relevance and utility in clinical settings.", "OLIGOSACÁRIDOS:Oligosaccharides are carbohydrates that can cause digestive issues for some people, often discussed in the context of dietary restrictions.", "SORBITE:Sorbitol is a sugar alcohol used as a sweetener that can cause digestive issues for some people.", "ARROZ:ARROZ, commonly known as rice, is a cereal that is safe for patients with celiac disease, as it does not contain gluten. It is recognized as a staple food and is often recommended for individuals with gluten intolerance. Additionally, rice is permitted in modified diets and is categorized as part of the cereal group, making it a versatile and essential component of many dietary plans.", "MAÍZ:MAÍZ, commonly known as corn, is a gluten-free cereal grain that is safe for individuals with celiac disease. It is widely used in various food products due to its gluten-free properties. In Spanish, it is also referred to as \"el maíz,\" emphasizing that it is a cereal that does not contain gluten, making it a suitable option for patients with celiac disease.", "MIJO:Millet is a gluten-free grain that is often included in diets for those with gluten intolerance.", "POLENTA:Polenta is a dish made from cornmeal that is gluten-free and suitable for those with gluten sensitivity.", "QUINOA:Quinoa is a gluten-free grain that is highly regarded for its nutritional benefits, particularly its high protein content. It is commonly used in products specifically designed for individuals with celiac disease, making it a popular choice for gluten-free diets